ext{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(3-0)^{2}+(5-5)^{2}+(4-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+9+0+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369352 13194139535838 true] [17592186369351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369353