ector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139535838 true] [17592186369364 1113 #uuid "54fe32be-53ae-55c1-bdf3-064634d40b4c" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369364 1145 "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,3\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}\\sqrt{3\\cdot 8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{3})≈{19.47}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." 13194139535838 true] [17592186369365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369366 13194139535838 true] [17592186369365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369367 13194139535838 true] [17592186369365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369368 13194139535838 true] [17592186369365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369369 13194139535838 true] [17592186369365 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369370 13194139535838 true] [17592186369365 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535838 true] [17592186369365 1041 "selection" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369365 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369366 13194139535838 true] [17592186369365 1110 #uuid "b28da0ea-38d9-5b50-b8dd-aa7d0bdc12a2" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369366 1034 "{19.47}^{∘}" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535838 true] [17592186369366 1111 #uuid "9a072932-26b9-56ea-b1b9-d577630f78ea" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369367 1034 "{32.54}^{∘}" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535838 true] [17592186369367 1111 #uuid "456fb80b-4f23-583e-8981-7131042a6096" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369368 1034 "{45.77}^{∘}" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369368 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535838 true] [17592186369368 1111 #uuid "144daa9b-0b6c-5296-b492-7cf4a67b6646" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369369 1034 "{21}^{∘}" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535838 true] [17592186369369 1111 #uuid "8af40672-e0ba-573c-8071-00ca71ec7b83" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369370 1034 "{37}^{∘}" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369370 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535838 true] [17592186369370 1111 #uuid "3459e90e-5976-5703-b769-16dcfff6e116" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369371 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369372 13194139535838 true] [17592186369371 1089 "q-86844" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369371 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535838 true] [17592186369371 1100 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369371 1113 #uuid "953a99ad-c0c2-51c8-971f-e6b5efdaa5df" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369371 1145 "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369373 13194139535838 true] [17592186369372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369374 13194139535838 true] [17592186369372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369375 13194139535838 true] [17592186369372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369376 13194139535838 true] [17592186369372 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369377 13194139535838 true] [17592186369372 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535838 true] [17592186369372 1041 "selection" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369372 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369377 13194139535838 true] [17592186369372 1110 #uuid "748ec448-a33b-5f0f-bd63-dadc1df15e17" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369373 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535838 true] [17592186369373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535838 true] [17592186369373 1111 #uuid "925dfb05-7f5b-54b3-9be2-c1d7e108f60b" 13194139535838 true] [175921863